## SQ-PRV-01 | a dedicated server with `enforce-secure-profile=true` lets a keyless client in
@group A
@commands set `enforce-secure-profile=true` in server.properties, boot; check `[privacy] acceptUnsignedChat = true` in config/creativecommon-common.toml; join with the pack client (PRV-01)
@pass the client joins and can chat; no "Missing profile public key" kick; latest.log has no mixin apply error for DedicatedServerUnsignedChatMixin
@fails the mixin not applied (server mixin list), or the common config not loaded when the first login arrives
@draft server side of the chat key block; needs one client join
## CQ-PRV-02 | the client starts with the user API offline and no key
@group client
@commands start the client (real account); `grep -E "Mojang user API (offline|online)|profile key pair" logs/latest.log` (PRV-02)
@pass one line "Mojang user API offline ([privacy] blockMojangReporting = true)"; no "Failed to retrieve profile key pair" error; login, skins and the multiplayer list work
@fails the mixin not applied: no state line, or a key fetch error from the offline service
@draft startup log check
## CQ-PRV-03 | chat on the pack's server shows no unsigned markers
@group client
@commands join the pack's server (SQ-PRV-01 setup), send a chat line from two players; watch for toasts on join (PRV-03)
@pass no "Chat messages can't be verified" toast; chat lines have no gray "Not Secure" bar; server-modified lines still show their tag
@fails the toast or bar still shown: UnsecureServerToastMixin or ChatNotSecureTagMixin not applied
@draft visual check, owner or runner screenshot
## CQ-PRV-04 | nothing can be reported
@group client
@commands on the pack's server, open Social Interactions (P), pick another player (PRV-04)
@pass the Report button is greyed out (reporting unavailable); no network error toast
@fails Report enabled: the user API is not the offline one
@draft vanilla report screen
## CQ-PRV-05 | the switch turns vanilla back on
@group client
@commands set `[privacy] blockMojangReporting = false` in config/creativecommon-client.toml, restart the client, join a server with `enforce-secure-profile=true` and `[privacy] acceptUnsignedChat = false` (PRV-05)
@pass state line says "online"; the client gets a key and joins the enforcing server; chat is signed (no Not Secure bar); set back to true afterwards
@fails a cached decision: the switch is read once per start, so a restart is needed
@draft opt-out path
